1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,051
The work is delivered.

2
00:00:02,051 --> 00:00:03,652
The invoice is next.

3
00:00:03,652 --> 00:00:07,254
But did the delivery actually meet what was agreed?

4
00:00:07,254 --> 00:00:14,457
For freelancers and small teams, that answer is often buried across messages, test logs, and someone else’s memory.

5
00:00:15,783 --> 00:00:19,088
Milestone Desk brings those checkpoints into one place.

6
00:00:19,088 --> 00:00:23,632
Start with the agreed milestones, their amounts, and their acceptance criteria.

7
00:00:23,632 --> 00:00:27,350
This is the running application, using a fictional project.

8
00:00:27,350 --> 00:00:33,134
The interactive grid lets you search the work and choose exactly what to review.

9
00:00:34,450 --> 00:00:37,800
Here is the promised outcome, alongside the delivery evidence.

10
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:42,638
A test log or handover note gives the reviewer something concrete to inspect.

11
00:00:42,638 --> 00:00:45,988
The app treats that text as a supplied claim.

12
00:00:45,988 --> 00:00:49,710
It does not pretend to have run the tests itself.

13
00:00:51,017 --> 00:00:54,868
These saved suggestions came from a real AI review.

14
00:00:54,868 --> 00:01:00,004
Each criterion is connected to an exact excerpt from the original evidence.

15
00:01:00,004 --> 00:01:02,999
The server checks that every quotation exists.

16
00:01:02,999 --> 00:01:06,423
Invented quotations are rejected, and gaps remain visible.

17
00:01:06,423 --> 00:01:10,703
The model helps you read; it cannot accept the work.

18
00:01:12,017 --> 00:01:16,625
The final decision belongs to a person, criterion by criterion.

19
00:01:16,625 --> 00:01:22,154
On another milestone, I can ask for more evidence and explain why.

20
00:01:22,154 --> 00:01:23,997
This example stays unsaved.

21
00:01:23,997 --> 00:01:28,605
Until every criterion is accepted, the invoice step remains locked.

22
00:01:28,605 --> 00:01:31,831
An optimistic AI summary cannot unlock it.

23
00:01:33,150 --> 00:01:38,330
For accepted work, Milestone Desk can prepare an unsent PayPal sandbox draft.

24
00:01:38,330 --> 00:01:40,057
This one already exists.

25
00:01:40,057 --> 00:01:47,395
Now we check it again against the actual sandbox, matching the invoice, recipient, amount, and draft status.

26
00:01:47,395 --> 00:01:51,711
Nothing is sent, and this recording creates no new invoice.

27
00:01:53,017 --> 00:02:02,074
Milestone Desk turns a vague handover into a review trail you can explain: the evidence, the human decision, and the verified draft.

28
00:02:02,074 --> 00:02:03,720
AI assists the review.

29
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:05,779
You remain responsible for acceptance.

30
00:02:05,779 --> 00:02:07,837
That is proof before payment.
